<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25858" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lapso</span></b> , āre, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. freq. n.</i> [id.], <i>to slip, slide, stumble, fall</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b> (<b>poet.</b> and in
			postAug. prose): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">(Priamum) in multo lapsantem sanguine nati,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 2, 551</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sanguine suo et lubrico paludum lapsantes
					(equi),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					1, 65</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lapsantibus equis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. H.
					1, 79</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lapsantem gressum firmare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					3, 632</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Flor. 2, 10, 3</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gyan vidi lapsare cruentae Vulnere Myrmidonis,</span>”
				<i>fall</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 5, 223</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">plantis lapsantibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 14, 2, 6</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b> (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">verba lapsantia,</span>”
				i. e. <i>babbled forth</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					1, 15, 1</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
